    <data name="Shell_PrivacyScope.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Applies to JPG Spinner 2.0 by Hadden Industries Ltd. Last updated: 26 October 2026. This notice describes this version of the app; the historical Store version may behave differently.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacySummary.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Your photos are processed on your device. JPG Spinner has no image-upload service, advertising, account system or custom network telemetry. Diagnostic records stay on your device unless you choose to export and share them.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyProcessingHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Photos and local processing</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyLocalDataHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Settings, folder access and recovery</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyChoices.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>You choose the source folder, processing options and whether to start reviewed work. You can change preferences in Settings and manage Windows app permissions in Windows Settings. Manage photos, exported files and backups in their chosen folders. Keep recovery data and backups until interrupted work is reconciled and you no longer need recovery; deleting them can prevent recovery. Uninstalling or resetting an app is not a substitute for deleting copies or exports in other folders.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyDiagnosticsHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Local diagnostics and retention</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyDiagnosticExclusions.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>These records exclude filenames, paths, photo bytes, thumbnails, Exif/XMP/IPTC metadata, GPS coordinates, arbitrary native exception messages, network endpoints and stable device identifiers. Windows crash reports are separate from these app diagnostic records.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyRetention.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Diagnostic storage is limited by size and file count, rather than a fixed number of days: at most 256 KiB and 64 retained record files, with each record at most 4,096 bytes. The reserved pending slot counts toward the storage budget and is never exported; the empty writer lease is not a record. Rotation removes only recognized, validated diagnostic records. Unknown, corrupt or unsupported files are preserved and cause logging or export to refuse rather than silently delete or disclose them. A logging failure does not fail image processing.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyExportHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Exporting and sharing diagnostics</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyExport.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Export local diagnostics asks you to choose a destination using the Windows file picker. It exports a bounded, revalidated snapshot of sanitized records, not arbitrary files from the diagnostic folder. Nothing is submitted automatically. Review the export before sharing: times, outcomes and resource limits can still be sensitive. You control who receives it and when to delete it. A failed or cancelled export may leave a partial file at the chosen destination; export is not guaranteed to be atomic.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyExternalHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Windows, cloud providers and websites</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyContactHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Questions and information you share with us</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyContact.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>For app privacy questions, contact Hadden Industries Ltd at info@haddenindustries.com. The publisher cannot retrieve photos or diagnostic files kept only on your device. If you contact us or choose to send us an export, that correspondence and any information you include are handled under the publisher's separate privacy policy, linked below. Do not send recovery journals, photos or other personal information unless you intend to share them.</value>
    </data>
</root>
